# Purpose
# Build the GitHub Pages compatible Jekyll site into _site.
#
# Common usage
# Run from the repository root.
# .\scripts\build-pages.ps1
# .\scripts\build-pages.ps1 -SkipSetup
# .\scripts\build-pages.ps1 -SkipSetup -NoClean
#
# Useful options
# -SkipSetup uses the existing Ruby bundle and skips dependency setup.
# -NoClean keeps the current _site folder before building.
# -Environment sets JEKYLL_ENV for the build.
#
# Recommended next command
# .\scripts\smoke-pages.ps1 -SkipBuild -Port 4000
#
# Notes
# This script writes the generated site to _site.
# Use pages-local.ps1 when you want the wrapper workflow.
